comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T21:22:58.543Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-10: reused canonical verdict item after all-status duplicate search. This tranche appends structured gate evaluations to the verified _workspace history stream and exposes queryable receipts without caller-supplied identity."
  "2026-08-10T23:01:06.034Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-11: persisted gate evaluations append structured assurance_verdict records to the verified workspace history stream with gate, trigger, judged tree or commit, per-assertion values, verdict, compute cost, and detected provenance. The SDK exposes bounded durable verdict queries, dry runs do not append, and integration acceptance proved a persisted verdict remains queryable in a fresh process. History verification and the full exact-coverage suite passed."
  "2026-08-10T23:31:46.122Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review work 2026-08-11 Europe/Vienna (PM event timestamps remain UTC): actively reconciling the non-dry verdict persistence contract, bounding verdict reads, and extending durable-history integration proof."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:43.625Z","harness:codex","Exact-head completion evidence 2026-08-11: reconciled the contract to persist every non-dry evaluation while dry runs remain non-persisting; verdict reads are newest-first and bounded to 50 by default with a 1,000 maximum. Packed npx dry-run acceptance preserved the verdict count and bunx persisted a passing verdict whose --limit 1 query returned exactly one newest record."
  "2026-08-11T02:02:17.710Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review completion 2026-08-11: verdict limits outside 1..1000 now fail at the transport boundary with the same usage exit class as non-integer input, while the direct SDK retains its typed range guard. Manual isolated CLI acceptance confirmed invalid limit exit 2 and valid bounded reads."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:01:06.703Z","harness:codex","Workspace-level assurance evidence belongs in the same verified append-only substrate as item history but under a dedicated workspace stream, so durable non-item records gain replay integrity without inventing synthetic work items."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:44.123Z","harness:codex",Durable verdict APIs should bound and order at the storage boundary; dry-run receipts remain useful evidence only when their non-persistence is explicit and tested across fresh processes.
